[{"id":4058755414,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7x67FW","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally (including runtime loading support), it works as expected. Code and documentation look good to me.\n\nI did a test on the TPS demo where I replaced its soundtrack (112 Kb/s Vorbis, 3 minutes of audio, 2.6 MB total) with Opus-encoded versions (64 Kb/s Opus). This provides a 1.3 MB size reduction, which stays roughly intact in the exported PCK size:\n\n- `master` with Vorbis soundtrack: 582,804 bytes\n- This PR with Opus soundtrack: 581,692 bytes (-1,112 KB)\n\nThe same goes in an exported ZIP data pack (therefore with compression):\n\n- `master` with Vorbis soundtrack: 252,776 bytes\n- This PR with Opus soundtrack: 251,772 bytes (-1,004 KB)\n\nTip: Use this shell script to mass-convert Vorbis to Opus (run at project root):\n\n```bash\nshopt -s globstar nullglob\nfor audio in **/*.ogg; do\n  ffmpeg -hide_banner -i $audio -b:a 64k ${audio//.ogg/.opus} -y\ndone\n```\n\nRemember to assign the .opus files in AudioStreamPlayer nodes, and move the .ogg originals outside the project folder afterwards so that they're not included in the exported PCK.\n\nFor best results, you should encode Opus audio from a lossless source (WAV or FLAC), as encoding from a lossy codec to another will make the loss of quality more significant. 64 Kb/s Opus should be equivalent to 128 Kb/s Vorbis when both are encoded from a lossless source, but this may not hold true when re-encoding lossy Vorbis audio.\n\nThat said, I can't seem to build Godot with `builtin_opus=no` despite having installed `opus-devel opusfile-devel` from the Fedora 43 repositories:\n\n```\n[ 16%] In file included from modules/opus/audio_stream_ogg_opus.cpp:31:\nmodules/opus/audio_stream_ogg_opus.h:35:10: fatal error: include/opusfile.h: No such file or directory\n   35 | #include <include/opusfile.h>\n      |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nIn comparison, `builtin_libvorbis=no` works.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117921#pullrequestreview-4058755414","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117921","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117921#pullrequestreview-4058755414"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117921"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-04T18:47:33Z","commit_id":"499f0508a16688076b8de87ec4dbdedfe1188022"},{"id":4058763125,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7x6891","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?u=7e327c81e8a9552ea98ca69adcccac4a50657dd9&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api